---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BancResultats from "../../../components/BancResultats.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Model test bench — Le labo de Ludo"
  description="Language models measured overnight on the lab's three RTX 3060 cards: speed, video memory and three small quality tests, on one gaming card and on all three."
>
  <a class="back" href="/en/">&larr; all articles</a>

  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>Model test bench</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The question I ask every time a model comes out: does it run on a gaming
      card? So every night there is something new (an Ollama or llama.cpp
      release, a recent model on Hugging Face), the lab measures it on a single
      12 GB RTX 3060, then on all three. The numbers below are published by the
      bench itself, untouched.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Output: tokens generated per second. First token: delay for a short
      question. The scores count correct answers to three small test suites:
      basic questions, tool calls like in Home Assistant, and Québécois French
      (raw score, the test is sometimes wrong). How the bench works:
      <a href="/en/blog/banc-dessai/">Bob's article</a>.
    </p>
  </header>

  <BancResultats lang="en" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }

  .lede,
  .note {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
